{"task":"transcribe","language":"en","duration":154.368,"text":"In particular, I need your help thinking through some of the technical considerations for this implementation. Some of the concerns I want your help addressing is while I do have some of the parameters like the window size and the amount of overlap, what is a good efficient way to handle the windowing of the EEG data before feeding so we can process the FFT efficiently across the entire signal. I also want to figure out how much, if at all, I should downsample the signal first because for the DSA, I think the upper limit of the frequency we're allowing them to configure is 70 hertz. I might be wrong about that, double check against the confluence document. But at that frequency, we would really only need a sampling frequency of 120 hertz, according to a Nyquist theorem. And so we might be able to get away with downsampling the signal to make it computationally more tractable to process it. Furthermore, the first thing I'm targeting is just the left hemisphere, right hemisphere spectrograms. And so we'll have groups of electrodes in each hemisphere. And I need to figure out how to handle the combination of those electrodes so that we can actually plot a single heat map. And I'm not sure whether I should average beforehand or before the FFT or like average the FFT components afterwards. And so help thinking through that would be very beneficial as well. My main goal is to try and replicate what Persist does in the way they produce their results. And so I would like for you to think through this problem and give me feedback on the different design considerations. And once you've like gone through each of them, any things you think I should think about or highlight in terms of the like configuration and then just a simple Python script that's more like proof of concept. We don't have to have a finalized clean API for any of it yet. Just something I can like iterate on and use as a starting point for the implementation.","segments":[{"id":0,"start":0.48,"end":7.84,"text":"In particular, I need your help thinking through some of the technical considerations for this implementation."},{"id":1,"start":8.48,"end":33.12,"text":"Some of the concerns I want your help addressing is while I do have some of the parameters like the window size and the amount of overlap, what is a good efficient way to handle the windowing of the EEG data before feeding so we can process the FFT efficiently across the entire signal."},{"id":2,"start":33.44,"end":47.52,"text":"I also want to figure out how much, if at all, I should downsample the signal first because for the DSA, I think the upper limit of the frequency we're allowing them to configure is 70 hertz."},{"id":3,"start":47.84,"end":53.68,"text":"I might be wrong about that, double check against the confluence document."},{"id":4,"start":54.32,"end":65.44,"text":"But at that frequency, we would really only need a sampling frequency of 120 hertz, according to a Nyquist theorem."},{"id":5,"start":65.76,"end":72.08,"text":"And so we might be able to get away with downsampling the signal to make it computationally more tractable to process it."},{"id":6,"start":72.64,"end":82.8,"text":"Furthermore, the first thing I'm targeting is just the left hemisphere, right hemisphere spectrograms."},{"id":7,"start":82.96000000000001,"end":89.04,"text":"And so we'll have groups of electrodes in each hemisphere."},{"id":8,"start":89.36,"end":98.16,"text":"And I need to figure out how to handle the combination of those electrodes so that we can actually plot a single heat map."},{"id":9,"start":98.48,"end":107.76,"text":"And I'm not sure whether I should average beforehand or before the FFT or like average the FFT components afterwards."},{"id":10,"start":108.72,"end":114.48,"text":"And so help thinking through that would be very beneficial as well."},{"id":11,"start":115.60000000000001,"end":121.76,"text":"My main goal is to try and replicate what Persist does in the way they produce their results."},{"id":12,"start":122.08,"end":128.88,"text":"And so I would like for you to think through this problem and give me feedback on the different design considerations."},{"id":13,"start":129.2,"end":144.32,"text":"And once you've like gone through each of them, any things you think I should think about or highlight in terms of the like configuration and then just a simple Python script that's more like proof of concept."},{"id":14,"start":144.48,"end":147.92000000000002,"text":"We don't have to have a finalized clean API for any of it yet."},{"id":15,"start":148.48,"end":154.08,"text":"Just something I can like iterate on and use as a starting point for the implementation."}]}